dsv41 patch 0050 (20.10.2026): the mHC overlap path's token bound as an environment switch.
V4.1's overlapped mHC (patch 0014: mix statistics on a side stream in FULL decode graphs) is taken only for windows of
at most MHC_OVERLAP_MAX_TOKENS = 16 rows (tuned on GB200 TP4). A 4-stream DSpark round (k = 4) has 20 rows and runs
the non-overlapped fused path instead: mhc_fused_tilelang on the main stream, GEMM included (profile of 19.10.2026 at 4 streams: mHC
3.35 ms a round, mhc_fused_tilelang_kernel 2.37 ms). VLLM_DSV41_MHC_OVERLAP_MAX_TOKENS=24 sends 17-24-row windows through the
overlap path too, so with patch 0048 their main stream keeps one launch a boundary. Rounding class for those windows
only (the overlap path's TF32 DeepGEMM mixes + TileLang epilogues, the kernels 1-3-stream rounds already run); 1-16
rows unchanged. The bound is read at import (model.py imports the constant); needs a serve restart.
Measured (20.10.2026, GB10, 2000 MHz, 0048 + 0050 against neither, T = 1): 4 streams code +3.9 %, prose +4.6 %,
JSON -0.1 %; 3 streams (15 rows, not affected by 0050) +0.0 ... +1.7 %; geometric mean +1.86 % (0048 alone: +0.99 %).
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_MHC_OVERLAP_MAX_TOKENS (default 16 = as before); we use 24.

--- a/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/ops/mhc.py
+++ b/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/ops/mhc.py
@@ -35,7 +35,9 @@
 logger = init_logger(__name__)
 
 # GB200 TP4/FlashInfer improves through 16 tokens; larger screens tie or regress.
-MHC_OVERLAP_MAX_TOKENS = 16
+# dsv41 patch 0050: VLLM_DSV41_MHC_OVERLAP_MAX_TOKENS raises the bound on GB10 (unmeasured there; with 0048 the main
+# stream keeps one launch a boundary, and 4-stream verify windows are 20 rows). Default 16 = unchanged.
+MHC_OVERLAP_MAX_TOKENS = int(os.environ.get("VLLM_DSV41_MHC_OVERLAP_MAX_TOKENS", "16"))
 
 # The fused all-reduce + mHC kernel of the overlap path, built once by
 # init_mhc_all_reduce.
